Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) systems often organize text chunks, entities, and evidence in flat retrieval spaces, which can separate global contextual semantics from fine-grained factual relations. This paper presents HoloHyper RAG, a cascaded multi-granularity hypergraph framework for knowledge-intensive question answering. The proposed framework models topics, chunks, sentences, and sentence-level entities as nested semantic units and constructs asymmetric bidirectional representations through local attention fusion. On the query side, HoloHyper RAG performs topic alignment, query-side cascaded enhancement, entity-aware reranking, and shared-entity multi-hop expansion to reduce semantic drift and recover distributed evidence. Experiments on machine-tool and general-domain datasets compare the proposed framework with representative RAG baselines under multiple LLM backbones. The results support the effectiveness of hierarchical hypergraph modeling for improving evidence organization, cross-domain robustness, and multi-hop retrieval in RAG systems.
